cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "llm-distill-watermark: payload-carrying ownership watermarks for LLM weights via LoRA-injected fictitious knowledge"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: rickgwei
    alias: rickgwei
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-08-18
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/rickgwei/llm-distill-watermark"
url: "https://github.com/rickgwei/llm-distill-watermark"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - model watermarking
  - model fingerprinting
  - LoRA
  - ownership verification
  - evaluation
abstract: >-
  A payload-carrying ownership watermark for LLM weights: a 64-bit payload
  (owner, recipient, version, CRC) is Reed-Solomon encoded into 32 codebook
  symbols realised as fictitious entities x attributes, embedded with a LoRA
  adapter and verified black-box with ordinary questions. Ships with an
  evaluation suite (effectiveness, harmlessness, capability, robustness,
  reliability), packaged evaluation datasets and an open attack suite.
